## Evidence

Tracked `.jig/` authority now contains schema-20 repository policy, the graph
taxonomy, CSpell dictionaries/configuration, Markdown policy, Python/Rust
validator configuration, exact tool/version projections, and the Rust toolchain
projection. `jig graph --root . --refresh` compiles the configured taxonomy with
zero parse issues, and `jig doctor --root .` reports `status: ready`, graph
state
`ready`, and version evidence for all nine configured tools.

The audit exposed two stale Python wrapper projections whose absolute recovery
environment no longer existed. They were replaced with direct repository-local
`pytest.exe` and `ruff.exe` paths. The tracked validation bootstrap at
`tools/validation/adapter-inbound/python_dependencies.py`
materializes that ignored environment from Jig's exact source-linked CPython
3.14.6 using explicit pytest/Ruff and transitive dependency pins, with rollback
when replacement fails. No global Python packages are installed.

Canonical pytest now includes every tracked Python test root: architecture,
packaging, Unreal editor-control, and Unreal project. An architecture guard
compares filesystem roots with `validation.pytest.args`, pins direct Python tool
paths, and preserves the source-linked Jig tool boundary.

A full `jig validate --fail-fast --root .` after these changes passes CSpell,
Markdownlint, all configured pytest roots, Ruff, nightly Clippy/rustfmt/tests,
stable Rust check, and Jig-native rules. The only remaining diagnostic is the
pre-existing published-history `JIG-COMMIT-013` for commit `13fc6414`; this task
does not rewrite historical commits to manufacture a green result.
